1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,612
Behind SK hynix,

2
00:00:01,632 --> 00:00:04,398
one company quietly took 10% of the market

3
00:00:04,418 --> 00:00:07,523
It's China's ChangXin Memory, known as CXMT

4
00:00:07,543 --> 00:00:12,794
Q2 DRAM share: Samsung 38%, SK hynix 25%, Micron 24%

5
00:00:12,814 --> 00:00:15,561
And CXMT is already at 10%

6
00:00:15,581 --> 00:00:19,249
While Samsung and SK hynix shifted their fabs to AI memory (HBM),

7
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:22,783
CXMT moved into the conventional DRAM market with cheap prices

8
00:00:22,803 --> 00:00:26,732
CXMT's HBM is still 2–4 years behind, so it's no immediate threat

9
00:00:26,752 --> 00:00:28,899
The problem is conventional DRAM prices

10
00:00:28,919 --> 00:00:30,180
SK hynix's profit this year

11
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:32,862
didn't come from selling more, but from selling at higher prices

12
00:00:32,882 --> 00:00:38,146
If CXMT fills that gap cheaply, prices could be the first to fall

13
00:00:38,166 --> 00:00:42,235
